%description:
FlatReceiverBase: the reception decision needs a packet error rate

An error model that returns a NaN packet error rate cannot decide whether a reception is successful. The receiver stops the run at the first frame with an error that names the error model, instead of deciding on NaN (before, the assertion failed in a debug build, and every frame was lost silently in a release build).

Two ad-hoc IEEE 802.11 hosts, 20 m apart, multicast frames.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
**.radio.receiver.errorModel.typename = "inet.test.moduletest.lib.ConstantRatesErrorModel"
include ../../lib/stochastic-errormodel-80211.ini

%exitcode: 1
%postrun-command: grep -h '<!>' test.out test.err > errors.out || true
%contains: errors.out
Error model inet::ConstantRatesErrorModel cannot provide the packet error rate that the reception decision requires
